<div class="wrap prose"><h1 class="ph">How it works</h1>
<p class="lead">SkillMaxx answers one question: <em>will this skill work in my agent, and what's the install command?</em> Here's exactly how we answer it, and where we stop short.</p>
<h2>1. Where the data comes from</h2><ul>
<li>Anthropic's official Claude Code plugin marketplace</li><li>OpenAI's official Codex plugin marketplace</li><li>xAI's official Grok Build plugin marketplace</li><li>The official MCP reference servers</li><li>MCP server packages published on npm</li></ul>
<h2>2. What the statuses mean</h2>
<p><span class="st documented">✓ Verified from docs</span>: an official source (the agent's own docs or marketplace) publishes the install method. Every one of these links to that source on the skill's page.</p>
<p><span class="st unknown">Not yet tested</span>: we found no official docs for that agent. It may still work. If you know it does, <a href="/submit/">tell us</a>.</p>
<p><span class="st tested">Tested ✓</span>: our test harness installed it in that agent's real CLI, inside a throwaway sandbox with an empty home folder and no accounts or API keys, and the agent then listed it as enabled or loaded. For MCP servers, the agent's own health check had to connect.</p>
<p><span class="st failed">✕ Failed</span>: the install or load check didn't pass. Common reasons are a required account, API key or extra arguments. Every result shows its date and a log excerpt.</p>
